INT. SNOW-BOUND ONSEN BATHHOUSE - NIGHT

Steam rolls off a cedar-lined pool. Paper lanterns. Snow falls past open shutters. The air smells of sulfur and pine.

KENJI (30s, lean, towel around his neck, glasses fogged) perches on the pool's edge. LUCIA (30s, copper hair pinned up, wrapped in a thin yukata) wades toward him, waist-deep.

MRS. TANABE (70s, bent, white apron) shuffles past with a tray of sake. DESMOND (40s, loud tourist, Hawaiian shirt under a parka) hovers at the door with a camera.

KENJI
You came all the way from Lisbon for a bath?

LUCIA
For you.

KENJI
That's the worst line I've ever heard.

LUCIA
It's the truest.

She reaches him. He wipes his glasses. She takes them. Holds them up to the lantern. He squints at her.

MRS. TANABE
Sake?

KENJI
Yes, please.

LUCIA
Obrigada.

MRS. TANABE
(sets the tray down)
He talks about you in his sleep.

KENJI
Mrs. Tanabe!

LUCIA
In which language?

MRS. TANABE
Bad Portuguese.

Lucia and Kenji laugh together. Their shoulders touch. Neither moves away.

DESMOND
Say cheese!

He lifts the camera. The flash pops. Lucia yelps. Kenji flinches. Both slip and splash into the pool. Mrs. Tanabe sighs and takes the camera from Desmond.

DESMOND (CONT'D)
Sorry! Sorry!

MRS. TANABE
Out. Now.

He leaves, bowing. Steam closes behind him.

Kenji surfaces, spluttering. Lucia surfaces beside him, hair loose, laughing. They look at each other for a long moment. Mrs. Tanabe turns and shuffles out, tray in hand, smiling at the floor.
